Vendored third-party dependency
===============================

  Library:  poseidon (Noir)
  Upstream: https://github.com/noir-lang/poseidon
  Tag:      v0.2.0
  Commit:   4bc50d88dd8d94a00a95730fd76501e676417abf
  License:  Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE)

Copied verbatim from NethermindEth/rs-soroban-ultrahonk@c2160987
(circuits/vendor/poseidon), which vendors the commit above unmodified; it is
also byte-identical to a fresh nargo checkout of the v0.2.0 tag. Only the
upstream repository's build/CI scaffolding is omitted (none of it is compiled
by nargo).

Why vendored: a git dependency names a mutable tag, and nargo has no `rev`
key and writes no lockfile, so a rebuild could fetch different library
source from unchanged repository source and produce a different ACIR and
verification key (OpenZeppelin's audit of the verifier repository, finding
N-06). A path dependency freezes the source in the repository.

CHECKSUMS.sha256 pins every vendored file;
crates/perch-zk-adapter/tests/vendor.rs fails on any drift. Changing this
library changes the verification key of circuits/perch_zk_recovery (and
_d24): regenerate with `just zk-artifacts` and redeploy the adapter.
